This directory contains the QBSP, VIS and LIGHT source subset from ericw-tools v0.18.1,
commit b6e2431f29a1f5763d4aa5fa37cb06838580f41a.
Upstream: https://github.com/ericwa/ericw-tools

The upstream QBSP and common code is GPL-2.0-or-later; see UPSTREAM_README.md,
the copyright notices in the source files, and COPYING. No Embree code is
included. Three dynamic-index offsetof expressions were rewritten as standard offset plus
index times element size for compatibility with current GCC. Each tool is
compiled in its own C++ namespace: QBSP uses double vectors while VIS/LIGHT
use float vectors. For environments without Embree, the LIGHT BSP ray-tracing
backend is enabled and adapted to the current model-info interface. Embedded
VIS/LIGHT do not create fixed-named logs in the user's working directory.
The QBSP and common polygon winding ranges are raised from 65,536 to
1,048,576 units, with corresponding QBSP world bounds raised to 2,097,152.
The sector exporter allows source coordinates up to 1,047,552 units, leaving
space for wall shells, collision hulls, and headnode expansion. Sector
playtests use BSP2 because BSP29 stores node and leaf bounds as 16-bit values.
Coordinates around 100,000 have been exercised by sector compilation tests;
the full enlarged range is not a claim of uniform lighting/physics precision.
